Similarly for skill certificate, compliance certificate, equipment, service window: we need to assign them to schedule candidates; they may need to stay linked for subsequent steps like verify_loading_profile_nominal, stage_schedule_candidate, load_container_onto_leg, verify_loading_profile_nominal, equipment_reserved/confirmed, route_sequence_context_set/validated, constraint_applied, operator_alignment_confirmed, compliance_validation_complete, finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation. Many of these require the candidate to have those links (skill_certificate_linked, compliance_certificate_linked, equipment_linked, service_window_linked). So we need to keep them linked throughout the process for each schedule candidate. So we cannot release them until after finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation (which yields dispatch_ready). After that we still need candidate_vehicle_linked and candidate_dispatch_slot_linked for dispatch. The vehicle link is separate; we can allocate vehicle after finalize? Actually allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate requires candidate_task_profile_linked (we have from attach_task_profile) and dispatch_ready (from finalize). It does not require skill_certificate_linked etc. So after finalize, we can release skill, compliance, equipment, service window if needed, but we need to keep them until after finalize? The finalize action does not require them; it only requires compliance_validation_complete. So we can release them after compliance_validation_complete but before finalize? Actually finalize requires compliance_validation_complete, which is set by verify_compliance_certificate. That action requires operator_alignment_confirmed and candidate_compliance_certificate_linked. So we need compliance_certificate_linked at that point. After verify_compliance_certificate, we get compliance_validation_complete true, but compliance_certificate_linked remains true (action does not remove it). So we could release after verify_compliance_certificate but before finalize? finalize only needs compliance_validation_complete, not the link. So we can release compliance_certificate after verify_compliance_certificate, before finalize. Similarly for operator_alignment_confirmed: verify_compliance_certificate requires operator_alignment_confirmed; after that we get compliance_validation_complete. operator_alignment_confirmed remains true (action does not remove). finalize does not require operator_alignment_confirmed. So we can release operator after verify_compliance_certificate? But operator_alignment_confirmed may be needed for nothing else after. However we might need operator_alignment_confirmed for nothing else. So we can release operator after verify_compliance_certificate.

Skill certificate: used in verify_loading_profile_nominal (requires candidate_skill_certificate_linked). After that we get candidate_loading_verified. Then later steps may not need skill certificate. So we can release after verify_loading_profile_nominal.

